item.description:
flatMap in Depth flatMap is the most powerful transformation in the Streams API. It maps each element to a stream, then flattens all those streams into one continuous stream.
// Without flatMap — stream of lists Stream&lt;List&lt;String&gt;&gt; nested = Stream.of( Arrays.asList(&#34;a&#34;, &#34;b&#34;), Arrays.asList(&#34;c&#34;, &#34;d&#34;), Arrays.asList(&#34;e&#34;) ); // Stream&lt;String&gt;: &#34;a&#34;, &#34;b&#34;, &#34;c&#34;, &#34;d&#34;, &#34;e&#34; Stream&lt;String&gt; flat = nested.flatMap(Collection::stream); Practical flatMap Patterns Flatten orders into line items:
List&lt;LineItem&gt; allItems = orders.stream() .flatMap(order -&gt; order.

The Problem Optional Solves NullPointerException is the most common runtime exception in Java. The root cause is that null is used for two different things simultaneously:
&ldquo;This field has no value&rdquo; (intentional absence) &ldquo;This reference was never set&rdquo; (programming error) Callers can&rsquo;t tell which meaning applies without reading the documentation or source code. And nothing in the type system forces them to check.
// Java 7: what does null mean here?
